>  ARE the two commands on line one are equal, so  LLDDR = LLDDRDR??  I keep trying the more 'phonetic' spelling of these commands by using the second part. Are they the same ?

Yes, they have exactly the same effects.

>  Restrictions:
> 
>  	- Chi strike 1 can't be followed by power surge 2 (alias chi strike 2).
>  	- Dash 2 can't be followed by power surge 1 (alias chi strike 1).
> 
>  Dash 2? HUH? Surge 1? WTF??

The second way of performing "Dash", and the first way for "Power
surge".  The spoiler is very terse, but those two lines indicate the two
combinations of techniques that are ambiguous:

You can't do strike-then-surge by performing LLDDR (chi strike 1) then
DRDRDRDR (power surge 2), because that starts with LLDDRDR, which would
be interpreted as "Chi Strike 2" (plus some garbage on the end).

Similarly, Dash2-Surge1 is LL-DDRRDDRR, which starts with LLDDR and
therefore would be interpreted as "Chi Strike 1" (plus appended junk).

In either case, including any such unrecognised "garbage" would mean
that your blitz was rejected, so you stumble (and waste a move).

