If you're still confused, here's an example:  (tested in WizMode)

My monk is at level 15:  this means that he can perform up to three
techniques (2 + 15/10 = 3.5, round down).  So I type:

#technique
(choose (c) chain blitz)
 In what direction? [hykulnjb><] 
(towards the mastodon that I've just ^G-ed into existence)
 Enter Blitz Command[. to end]:  
RRLRLDDDD.

 You dash forwards!  You bump into a mastodon.
 (that was "RR" = Dash, a starter move)

 You let loose a barrage of blows!  You hit the mastodon!
 You hit the mastodon!  You hit the mastodon!  You kill the mastodon!
 (that was all from the "LRL" = Pummel, a chain move)

 You strike nothing.
 (that was "DDDD" = ground slam, a finisher, but the monster was already
 dead so it had no effect)


If you want to *memorize* the moves for each technique, without
resorting to note-taking (no matter how brief), it may help if you
picture the path that your character would take if you were to use those
movements in an empty room.  Or not.

